 "summary": {
  "version": 2,
  "basis": "em",
  "attribution": "Written by a model from the explanatory memorandum; not the record",
  "describes_version": "original",
  "as_of": "2024-02-07",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would appropriate money from the Consolidated Revenue Fund for the ordinary annual services of the government, adding to the 2023-24 Budget appropriations for decisions taken since the Budget.",
   "It would fund departmental items, administered items and corporate entity items for Commonwealth entities in the amounts listed in Schedule 1, with the detail in the Portfolio Additional Estimates Statements.",
   "It is one of three Additional Estimates Bills alongside Appropriation Bill (No. 4) and the Appropriation (Parliamentary Departments) Bill (No. 2) 2023-2024, would commence on Royal Assent and be repealed on 1 July 2026."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "The Advance to the Finance Minister under Appropriation Act (No. 1) 2023-2024 would be restored to its original $400 million limit after commencement.",
   "Where the Finance Minister has already advanced money for the same expenditure before commencement, the bill's appropriation for it would be reduced by that amount, but not below nil.",
   "Payments to corporate entities would be made from the fund by the relevant department and must be used for the purposes of those entities.",
   "Amounts for an item whose purpose matches a special account could be debited from the appropriation and credited to the special account.",
   "Notional transactions between non-corporate entities would be treated as real transactions that debit an appropriation.",
   "The Act would be repealed at the start of 1 July 2026."
  ],
  "affected": "Non-corporate Commonwealth entities, corporate Commonwealth entities and Commonwealth companies that receive appropriations, and the Finance Minister are affected.",
